LICENSE covers this repository's own contents: the Dockerfile, the build scripts, the Makefile, the workflows
and the docs. Nothing upstream is vendored here; every dependency is fetched at build time.

This file covers the ARTIFACT the repository publishes, namely the container image
(ghcr.io/yama6a/smartctl-exporter-multiarch). That image is an aggregate of separately licensed works, and
each keeps its own license.


Components of the published image
---------------------------------

  smartctl_exporter            Apache-2.0
    Source:  https://github.com/prometheus-community/smartctl_exporter at the tag named in the release's
             build-inputs.json. The published release binary is repackaged unmodified.

  smartmontools                GPL-2.0-or-later
    Source:  https://builds.sr.ht/~smartmontools or https://github.com/smartmontools/smartmontools
             Installed from the Alpine `smartmontools` package. Alpine's build recipe (APKBUILD) and the
             upstream tarball it fetches are at
             https://gitlab.alpinelinux.org/alpine/aports/-/tree/master/community/smartmontools
    Written offer: the corresponding source for the smartmontools binaries in a published image is the
             upstream release identified by `apk info -v smartmontools` inside that image, obtainable from
             the URLs above.

  Alpine Linux base image      MIT and others, per package
    Source:  https://gitlab.alpinelinux.org/alpine/aports
             The exact base is digest-pinned in versions.env and recorded in each release's
             build-inputs.json.


